    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YWjtKsLbFBfV3ynQseWxLE)_\n\n## What\n- **Org-sized posframe text.** `sp-minibuffer.el` hooks `sp-text-buffer` on `text-mode-hook`, which scales Org (and all text modes) up 4 `text-scale` steps, so the `default` face alone is smaller than Org text. New `sp-fonts-text-scale-steps` (4) is the single number for both. `sp-posframe--set-text-size` (replaces `sp-posframe--reset-text-scale` from #145) runs first on `minibuffer-setup-hook` (depth -90), drops all face remappings of the minibuffer, whatever buffer you called it from, and sets that scale.\n- **Dashboard box text.** `sp-fonts-dashboard-menu-height` (0.85) sets the height of `sp-dashboard-menu-face` relative to `default`. `sp-fonts-ui-faces` applies it when the dashboard loads, after a theme loads and on `fontaine-set-preset-hook`, so it follows the fontaine preset.\n- Docs and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). The root cause of the buffer-dependent size is not confirmed; the remapping reset is a defensive fix. Smaller menu text may shift box alignment (the box lines and art are laid out in columns of the base font); set `sp-fonts-dashboard-menu-height` to 1.0 to compare.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9cVX4xhp367pqb88n)_",
